   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off the side, plan and front views (tools/trace/a388/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. Its two full decks are one tall section: the crown, belly and plan width describe it (the front view's outline lies on the two quarter-ellipses each side, widest 0.2 m below the middle), and the upper deck's windows are their own row (cabin.upperWindows). The front view is drawn 3.6% smaller than the side (its printed 79.75 m span): evened out to the side's scale. The side view draws the fuselage 8.31 m tall against the printed 8.41 m, which the front view agrees with: fit to the printed height (fit_height.py). The side view draws the inlets 0.53 m and 0.76 m ahead of the printed 22.23 m and 29.94 m, the plan 0.37 m behind them: the nacelles are moved to the printed figures (build.py's rule). The cabin windows are the drawing's; the main deck's behind the wing and its fairing, and four upper-deck ones behind dimension lines and the wingtip fence, are placed at its 0.62 m pitch. The drawing shows four main-deck doors (M1, M2, M3 over the wing, and the aft one) and three upper-deck doors. Only the wingtip fence's upper blade is drawn (the format's device rises from the wing)."
